      "slug": "adacleargrasp",
      "short_name": "AdaClearGrasp",
      "title": "AdaClearGrasp: Learning Adaptive Clearing for Zero-Shot Robust Dexterous Grasping in Densely Cluttered Environments",
      "authors": "Zixuan Chen, Wenquan Zhang, Jing Fang, Ruiming Zeng, Zhixuan Xu, Yiwen Hou, Xinke Wang, Jieqi Shi, Jing Huo, Yang Gao",
      "year": 2026,
      "venue": "arXiv v1",
      "kind": "model",
      "category": "AM.MAN.DEX.AGENT",
      "related_categories": [
        "AM.MAN.DEX.POLICY.LEARNING"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "dexterous",
        "agent-architecture",
        "vlm",
        "task-planning",
        "adaptive-clearing",
        "cluttered-grasping",
        "skill-library",
        "model-context-protocol",
        "reinforcement-learning",
        "ppo",
        "geometry-aware-policy",
        "failure-recovery",
        "sim-to-real",
        "real-world"
      ],
      "tldr": {
        "zh": "AdaClearGrasp 让 VLM 根据场景和执行反馈决定直接抓取还是先推拉清障，通过 MCP 调用几何规划技能与 PPO 训练的 GeoGrasp 抓取策略，并在失败后重新规划，实现密集杂物中的目标抓取。",
        "en": "AdaClearGrasp uses a VLM to choose direct grasping or push/pull clearing from the scene and execution feedback, invokes geometric planning skills and a PPO-trained GeoGrasp policy through MCP, and replans after failures to grasp targets in dense clutter."
      },
      "evaluation_scope": {
        "zh": "上层 Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct 输出工具调用与参数，清障／复位采用几何规划，失败反馈修改后续技能选择。GeoGrasp 为 PPO 训练的 MLP：59 维观测包含 18 个手部关键点到物体最近点的归一化向量、目标高度和末端高度／姿态；输出 19 维关节增量（机械臂 7＋XHand 12），经 PD 执行。在无杂物环境中用 Cube、Cup、Apple 训练，评测未见物体与无需微调的真机迁移；真机为 xArm7＋XHand，几何观测依赖物体模型与 FoundationPose 位姿估计。配套 Clutter-Bench 含 7 个目标×3 个杂乱等级×10 个布局，共 210 个仿真场景；真机报告 18 个场景。",
        "en": "The Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct planner emits tool calls and parameters; geometric planners execute clearing/reset skills, and failure reports change subsequent skill selection. GeoGrasp is a PPO-trained MLP with 59-D observations: normalized nearest-point vectors from 18 hand keypoints, target height, and TCP height/orientation. It outputs 19 joint increments (7 arm + 12 XHand) executed by PD control. Training uses Cube, Cup and Apple without clutter; evaluation covers unseen objects and real-robot transfer without fine-tuning. Hardware uses xArm7 + XHand; geometric observations require object meshes and FoundationPose pose estimates. Clutter-Bench contains 7 targets × 3 clutter levels × 10 layouts = 210 simulation scenes; hardware evaluation reports 18 scenes."
      },
